<title>UK: FORECAST - Austerity working for EMU convergence.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Austerity working for EMU convergence.</headline>
<byline>Pratima Desai</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The fiscal austerity which countries have imposed upon themselves to meet entry targets for Europe's economic and monetary union (EMU) in January 1999 seems to be working, a Reuters survey showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Forecasts from 35 economists across Europe showed on average that 14 out of 15 European Union (EU) countries were moving closer to achieving or bettering the Maastricht convergence targets set for membership of EMU.</p>
